{"id":"QB-261031-2G2R","title":"Phiếu bài tập 03/10/2026","student":"","questions":[{"id":"SAT-CB-PT5-M2-Q17","ref":"SAT-CB-PT5-M2-Q17","label":"1","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"Which expression is equivalent to $(8x^3 + 8) - (x^3 - 2)$ ?","options":{"A":"$8x^3 + 6$","B":"$7x^3 + 10$","C":"$8x^3 + 10$","D":"$7x^3 + 6$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-J-M2-Q15","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-J-M2-Q15","label":"2","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The area of a triangle is $33$ square inches. The length of the base of the triangle, in inches, is the sum of $d$ and a positive number $14$, and the height, in inches, is $5$ less than $d$. What is the value of $d$?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025NOV-US-A-M1-Q14","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025NOV-US-A-M1-Q14","label":"3","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The scatterplot shows the relationship between $x$ and $y$. A line of best fit is also shown. Which of the following is closest to the slope of the line of best fit shown?","options":{"A":"$-1.84$","B":"$-0.54$","C":"$0.54$","D":"$1.84$"},"figures":[{"src":"data:image/png;base64,","alt":"Scatterplot with x from 0 to 5 and y from 0 to 5 (gridlines every 1). Four points: about (1, 0.3), (2, 1.7), (3, 2.6), (4, 2). A line of best fit starts at the origin (0, 0) and rises to the right, reaching about (5, 2.7)."}]},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-G-M2-Q21","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-G-M2-Q21","label":"4","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$b^2+4c=9d$<br><br>The given equation relates the real numbers $b$, $c$, and $d$, where $9d>4c$. Which equation correctly expresses $b$ in terms of $c$ and $d$?","options":{"A":"$b=\\frac{9d+4c}{2}$","B":"$b=\\frac{9d-4c}{2}$","C":"$b=\\pm\\sqrt{9d+4c}$","D":"$b=\\pm\\sqrt{9d-4c}$"}},{"id":"SAT-EQB-20261018-PSDA-Q19","ref":"SAT-EQB-20261018-PSDA-Q19","label":"5","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"To determine the mean number of children per household in a community, Tabitha surveyed $20$ families at a playground. For the $20$ families surveyed, the mean number of children per household was $2.4$. Which of the following statements must be true?","options":{"A":"The mean number of children per household in the community is $2.4$.","B":"A determination about the mean number of children per household in the community should not be made because the sample size is too small.","C":"The sampling method is flawed and may produce a biased estimate of the mean number of children per household in the community.","D":"The sampling method is not flawed and is likely to produce an unbiased estimate of the mean number of children per household in the community."}},{"id":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-SALG-Q115","ref":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-SALG-Q115","label":"6","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"A team of workers has been moving cargo off of a ship. The equation below models the approximate number of tons of cargo, $y$, that remains to be moved $x$ hours after the team started working.<br>$$y=120-25x$$<br>The graph of this equation in the $xy$-plane is a line. What is the best interpretation of the $x$-intercept in this context?","options":{"A":"The team will have moved all the cargo in about 4.8 hours.","B":"The team has been moving about 4.8 tons of cargo per hour.","C":"The team has been moving about 25 tons of cargo per hour.","D":"The team started with 120 tons of cargo to move."}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025MAR-INT-E-M1-Q07","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025MAR-INT-E-M1-Q07","label":"7","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"Circle N has a radius of $9$ millimeters (mm). Circle M has an area of $25\\pi$ mm$^2$. What is the total area, in mm$^2$, of circles N and M?","options":{"A":"$106\\pi$","B":"$61\\pi$","C":"$43\\pi$","D":"$14\\pi$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025MAY-INT-A-M1-Q21","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025MAY-INT-A-M1-Q21","label":"8","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"Hakim has a bag of $50$ tiles, where $45$ are labeled with a letter and $5$ are blank. If Hakim selects a tile from the bag at random, what is the probability of selecting a blank tile? (Express your answer as a decimal or fraction, not as a percent.)"},{"id":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-SALG-Q48","ref":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-SALG-Q48","label":"9","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$$y>2x-1$$<br>$$2x>5$$<br><br>Which of the following consists of the $y$-coordinates of all the points that satisfy the system of inequalities above?","options":{"A":"$y>6$","B":"$y>4$","C":"$y>\\frac{5}{2}$","D":"$y>\\frac{3}{2}$"}},{"id":"SAT-VN-20261003-M-Q142","ref":"SAT-VN-20261003-M-Q142","label":"10","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$4x^2+14=32x+r$. In the given equation, $r$ is a constant. The equation has exactly one real solution. What is the value of $r$?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025OCT-US-A-M1-Q13","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025OCT-US-A-M1-Q13","label":"11","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"A model estimates that the initial number of photons in an X-ray beam is $800$ when the beam reaches the surface of a certain material. The model also estimates that when the beam passes through this material, the number of photons in the beam decreases by $50\\%$ for each $7$ millimeters of the material the beam passes through. Which equation represents this model, where $I$ is the estimated number of photons in the beam when the beam reaches a point $x$ millimeters from the surface?","options":{"A":"$I=800(7)^{x/2}$","B":"$I=800(0.5)^{x}$","C":"$I=800(2)^{x/7}$","D":"$I=800(0.5)^{x/7}$"}},{"id":"SAT-EQB-20261018-SGT-Q26","ref":"SAT-EQB-20261018-SGT-Q26","label":"12","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"In the $xy$-plane, circle $M$ is the graph of the equation $(x-4)^2+(y-5)^2=9$. Circle $P$ has the same center as circle $M$ but has a radius that is twice the radius of circle $M$. Which equation represents circle $P$?","options":{"A":"$(x-4)^2+(y-5)^2=18$","B":"$(x-4)^2+(y-5)^2=36$","C":"$(x-8)^2+(y-10)^2=9$","D":"$(x-8)^2+(y-10)^2=18$"}},{"id":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-ADV-Q28","ref":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-ADV-Q28","label":"13","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"From 2005 through 2014, the number of music CDs sold in the United States declined each year by approximately $15\\%$ of the number sold the preceding year. In 2005, approximately $600$ million CDs were sold in the United States. Of the following, which best models $C$, the number of millions of CDs sold in the United States, $t$ years after 2005?","options":{"A":"$C=600(0.15)^t$","B":"$C=600(0.85)^t$","C":"$C=600(1.15)^t$","D":"$C=600(1.85)^t$"}},{"id":"PSAT-2024-PT2-M1-Q15","ref":"PSAT-2024-PT2-M1-Q15","label":"14","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$x = 3$<br>$y = (15 - x)^{2}$<br><br>A solution to the given system of equations is $(x, y)$. What is the value of $xy$ ?","options":{"A":"432","B":"54","C":"45","D":"18"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-INT-A-M2-Q12","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-INT-A-M2-Q12","label":"15","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$35x+3=k(7x+3)+7x$<br><br>In the given equation, $k$ is a constant. The equation has exactly one solution. Which value CANNOT be the value of $k$?","options":{"A":"$5$","B":"$4$","C":"$0$","D":"$-4$"}},{"id":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-ADV-Q102","ref":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-ADV-Q102","label":"16","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$$-16x^2-8x+c=0$$<br><br>In the given equation, $c$ is a constant. The equation has exactly one solution. What is the value of $c$?"},{"id":"PSAT-EQB-20261016-PILOT-Q13","ref":"PSAT-EQB-20261016-PILOT-Q13","label":"17","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"A factory makes $9$-inch, $7$-inch, and $4$-inch concrete screws. During a certain day, the number of $9$-inch concrete screws that the factory makes is $5$ times the number $n$ of $7$-inch concrete screws, and the number of $4$-inch concrete screws is $22$. During this day, the factory makes $100$ concrete screws total. Which equation represents this situation?","options":{"A":"$9 (5 n) + 7 n + 4 (22) = 100$","B":"$9 n + 7 n + 4 n = 100$","C":"$5 n + 22 = 100$","D":"$6 n + 22 = 100$"}},{"id":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-ADV-Q02","ref":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-ADV-Q02","label":"18","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$$\\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline x & f(x)\\\\\\hline 0 & 5\\\\\\hline 1 & \\frac{5}{2}\\\\\\hline 2 & \\frac{5}{4}\\\\\\hline 3 & \\frac{5}{8}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}$$<br><br>The table above gives the values of the function $f$ for some values of $x$. Which of the following equations could define $f$?","options":{"A":"$f(x)=5(2^{x+1})$","B":"$f(x)=5(2^{x})$","C":"$f(x)=5(2^{-(x+1)})$","D":"$f(x)=5(2^{-x})$"}},{"id":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-SALG-Q90","ref":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-SALG-Q90","label":"19","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$$y=2x-3$$<br>$$3y=5x$$<br><br>In the solution to the system of equations above, what is the value of $y$?","options":{"A":"$-15$","B":"$-9$","C":"$9$","D":"$15$"}},{"id":"SAT-SATLORDS-2026MAR-M2-Q37","ref":"SAT-SATLORDS-2026MAR-M2-Q37","label":"20","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"For the polynomial function $f$, the graph of $y = f(x)$ in the $xy$-plane passes through the points $(-3, 0)$, $(1, 0)$, and $(7, 0)$.\n\nWhich of the following must be a factor of $f(x)$?","options":{"A":"$x + 1$","B":"$x + 7$","C":"$x - 1$","D":"$x - 3$"}}]}